1
00:00:01,246 --> 00:00:07,530
[SPEAKER_01]: So, here's another question about the five hindrances.

2
00:00:08,151 --> 00:00:15,715
[SPEAKER_01]: Bhante, I see the five hindrances, or I've been contemplating them, as ways that I try to manage my suffering.

3
00:00:17,296 --> 00:00:29,805
[SPEAKER_01]: When I suffer, I get angry, I seek sensual pleasures, take on projects, pointless or not pointless, distract myself with entertainment, or sleep, or relentlessly,

4
00:00:30,644 --> 00:00:34,385
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, non-management of suffering is there.

5
00:00:34,405 --> 00:00:37,045
[SPEAKER_01]: But, first and foremost, that's not what hindrances are.

6
00:00:37,065 --> 00:00:41,726
[SPEAKER_01]: The whole thing that was described there, those are already the results of hindrances.

7
00:01:02,173 --> 00:01:04,835
[SPEAKER_00]: You don't engage with hindrances once you get angry.

8
00:01:05,476 --> 00:01:07,517
[SPEAKER_00]: Getting angry in the first place is already a hindrance.

9
00:01:09,779 --> 00:01:19,105
[SPEAKER_00]: So, liability to lust, liability to aversion, anger, liability to restlessness or worry or doubt, that's already a hindrance.

10
00:01:19,586 --> 00:01:26,491
[SPEAKER_00]: Those are already signs and features of hindrances, signs and secondary characteristics that you're not seeing.

11
00:01:27,411 --> 00:01:31,254
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you think the hindrances, when you're fully engaged with your desires and so on,

12
00:01:31,702 --> 00:01:37,383
[SPEAKER_00]: No, that's already like complete result of the proliferative hindrance that you are fully under.

13
00:01:39,844 --> 00:01:41,745
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you have to give up the management.

14
00:01:41,985 --> 00:01:43,025
[SPEAKER_00]: So, what do I do then?

15
00:01:43,125 --> 00:01:43,805
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, there you go.

16
00:01:43,845 --> 00:01:44,505
[SPEAKER_00]: What do you do then?

17
00:01:44,705 --> 00:01:45,466
[SPEAKER_00]: Question comes up.

18
00:01:45,606 --> 00:01:47,026
[SPEAKER_00]: Pressure to do something comes up.

19
00:01:47,086 --> 00:01:48,206
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, that's already a hindrance.

20
00:01:50,387 --> 00:01:51,387
[SPEAKER_00]: It's already going to be one.

21
00:01:51,407 --> 00:01:53,688
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you discern hindrance in whatever comes up.

22
00:01:57,549 --> 00:01:58,889
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you stop doing the management.

23
00:01:59,934 --> 00:02:07,920
[SPEAKER_00]: I bet your restlessness and anxiety would increase, because I have all this dukkha coming up and I'm not doing anything about it.

24
00:02:08,981 --> 00:02:10,502
[SPEAKER_00]: So, that's a pressure, isn't it?

25
00:02:11,863 --> 00:02:18,148
[SPEAKER_00]: That's an internal pressure that's trying to make you act, trying to get you to do, trying to pick it up, take the bait.

26
00:02:19,590 --> 00:02:20,490
[SPEAKER_00]: That's already a hindrance.

27
00:02:21,011 --> 00:02:25,174
[SPEAKER_00]: And if you pick it up, you stepped into it, right into the trap.

28
00:02:26,815 --> 00:02:27,135
[SPEAKER_00]: Doubt.

29
00:02:27,696 --> 00:02:28,997
[SPEAKER_00]: Doubt will come up, for sure.

30
00:02:31,155 --> 00:02:32,136
[SPEAKER_00]: But I'm not clear about this.

31
00:02:32,176 --> 00:02:32,917
[SPEAKER_00]: I'm not clear about that.

32
00:02:33,297 --> 00:02:34,137
[SPEAKER_00]: Pressure builds up.

33
00:02:35,158 --> 00:02:42,002
[SPEAKER_00]: You start seeking clarity out of that, acting out of that pressure, because the pressure is uncomfortable.

34
00:02:43,623 --> 00:02:44,784
[SPEAKER_00]: And yes, it's not going to be perfect.

35
00:02:44,804 --> 00:02:54,229
[SPEAKER_00]: You're bound to be doing it to some extent, but you want to be able to, like, hold on, acting out of pressure is what hinders me.

36
00:02:54,450 --> 00:02:58,272
[SPEAKER_00]: There is no external justification as to what I direct my actions for.

37
00:03:00,195 --> 00:03:11,362
[SPEAKER_00]: Sure, from the worldly point of view, there are better ways of acting out of hindrances and worse ways, but fundamentally, if you're trying to be free from hindrances, they're all the same.

38
00:03:12,122 --> 00:03:13,543
[SPEAKER_00]: Acting out of pressure means you're hindered.

39
00:03:14,423 --> 00:03:20,367
[SPEAKER_00]: So, that's when you start to recognize as well, okay, doubt, it pressures me, but it's not really about the clarity, the way it presents itself.

40
00:03:20,507 --> 00:03:21,888
[SPEAKER_00]: It's about acting out of pressure.

41
00:03:21,908 --> 00:03:24,129
[SPEAKER_00]: It's about getting rid of the discomfort of the pressure.

42
00:03:25,230 --> 00:03:25,930
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you abstain.

43
00:03:26,771 --> 00:03:28,592
[SPEAKER_00]: No, I will not seek for clarity and answers.

44
00:03:30,100 --> 00:03:31,841
[SPEAKER_00]: For as long as this pressure does not subside.

45
00:03:32,241 --> 00:03:36,942
[SPEAKER_00]: When the pressure subsides, I can try and seek, if truly I needed clarity and answers.

46
00:03:37,662 --> 00:03:49,066
[SPEAKER_00]: But often, after the pressure would have subsided, I don't know how long it would take, maybe days, you then find out that you already knew the answer, what you were seeking, supposedly seeking for.

47
00:03:49,426 --> 00:03:56,988
[SPEAKER_00]: And it was all just a, just a, just a, just a show, just mask, just sort of trying to hook you, bait you into acting out of pressure,

48
00:03:58,138 --> 00:04:01,440
[SPEAKER_00]: On a pretext of like a... oh, but this is a valid reason.

49
00:04:02,281 --> 00:04:03,601
[SPEAKER_00]: So, that's already acting out of hindrance.

50
00:04:03,621 --> 00:04:05,623
[SPEAKER_00]: You have loads to do when you stop doing the management.

51
00:04:06,563 --> 00:04:11,326
[SPEAKER_00]: But it will all be on the level of abstaining from doing that's rooted in pressure.

52
00:04:11,846 --> 00:04:23,093
[SPEAKER_00]: Discerning that, cultivating those perceptions of those signs and features that hint even before you are kind of down the rabbit hole of having no choice but to act out, type of thing.

53
00:04:27,650 --> 00:04:28,510
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, seeing your...

54
00:04:28,910 --> 00:04:33,091
[SPEAKER_01]: So, need to do something palpable is a hindrance already.

55
00:04:35,652 --> 00:04:38,333
[SPEAKER_01]: The pressure to... Well, of course, it's going to be... you're going to be pressured.

56
00:04:38,413 --> 00:04:39,773
[SPEAKER_01]: Then, there's the choosing of it.

57
00:04:40,493 --> 00:04:42,154
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, yeah.

58
00:04:42,174 --> 00:04:43,834
[SPEAKER_00]: But first, you accept the pressure.

59
00:04:45,275 --> 00:04:51,756
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, you automatically accept the pressure when you choose to act out of those... the sense of duty or whatever it's sort of trying to make you act.

60
00:04:52,176 --> 00:04:54,137
[SPEAKER_00]: Then, by not acting out, you're left with the pressure.

61
00:04:54,951 --> 00:04:55,492
[SPEAKER_00]: So, what do you do?

62
00:04:55,512 --> 00:04:56,232
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, that's what you do.

63
00:04:56,292 --> 00:04:57,774
[SPEAKER_00]: You endure that pressure on the right level.

64
00:04:58,254 --> 00:04:59,715
[SPEAKER_00]: You don't give in by body, by speech.

65
00:04:59,795 --> 00:05:05,760
[SPEAKER_00]: Mentally, you try to disassociate and unfocus from the thoughts that are trying to get your focus.

66
00:05:06,121 --> 00:05:12,626
[SPEAKER_00]: You know, as I said so many times before already, say you're pressured by ill-will.

67
00:05:13,667 --> 00:05:16,730
[SPEAKER_00]: Okay, you're not doing anything by body, you're not doing anything by speech.

68
00:05:18,051 --> 00:05:20,733
[SPEAKER_00]: Mentally, there are thoughts revolving around it.

69
00:05:21,174 --> 00:05:22,395
[SPEAKER_00]: But you are the one who then

70
00:05:23,038 --> 00:05:27,402
[SPEAKER_00]: Focuses your lens onto them, and that gives the momentum.

71
00:05:27,562 --> 00:05:34,147
[SPEAKER_00]: So, it's like... and in the same way, when people think, I must stop these thoughts, in order to stop them, you need to pick them up first.

72
00:05:34,427 --> 00:05:37,610
[SPEAKER_00]: So, either way, you focus on them in order to deal with them.

73
00:05:37,630 --> 00:05:39,151
[SPEAKER_00]: You're hooked.

74
00:05:39,171 --> 00:05:40,092
[SPEAKER_00]: You stepped into a trap.

75
00:05:40,793 --> 00:05:51,902
[SPEAKER_00]: So, on the mental level, regardless of the hindrance, when these thoughts are trying to crystallize themselves into sensual thoughts, or thoughts of ill-will, or thoughts of restlessness, that last part you don't do.

76
00:05:54,190 --> 00:05:54,650
[SPEAKER_00]: That's what it was.

77
00:05:54,690 --> 00:05:55,551
[SPEAKER_00]: He doesn't welcome.

78
00:05:55,611 --> 00:05:56,432
[SPEAKER_00]: He doesn't delight.

79
00:05:56,832 --> 00:05:58,493
[SPEAKER_00]: It's like, okay, these thoughts are trying to enter.

80
00:05:59,014 --> 00:06:07,340
[SPEAKER_00]: It's not my job, no duty, and it's actually gonna make me fall into a trap if I try to deal and prevent them or stop them.

81
00:06:07,900 --> 00:06:12,844
[SPEAKER_00]: But it is my job to not allow them to take that center stage of my focus, of my attention.

82
00:06:14,938 --> 00:06:18,040
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you want to know that they're there, and you already know that they're there.

83
00:06:18,160 --> 00:06:26,344
[SPEAKER_00]: As I said before, even before you allow thoughts to specifically crystallize in your mind, you know exactly what direction they will be crystallizing.

84
00:06:26,524 --> 00:06:27,984
[SPEAKER_00]: You know exactly what thoughts will be.

85
00:06:28,024 --> 00:06:30,566
[SPEAKER_00]: If it's lust, if it's anger, you know exactly where it's going to go.

86
00:06:31,066 --> 00:06:34,027
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you don't give that last push on that mental level.

87
00:06:34,487 --> 00:06:39,750
[SPEAKER_00]: And if that pressure for those thoughts to crystallize stays there with you for days, that's your training.

88
00:06:41,914 --> 00:06:50,360
[SPEAKER_00]: Not allowing that last drop of crystallization, of that focusing on them, but not completely trying to ignore what's happening.

89
00:06:50,380 --> 00:06:57,805
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, if you're doing it rightly, you won't be able to ignore it, because, obviously, the knowledge of what you're pressured towards, it is there, it is known.

90
00:06:59,026 --> 00:07:01,228
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you don't try to distract yourself from it either.

91
00:07:02,209 --> 00:07:04,750
[SPEAKER_00]: Or, let me do something, so I completely forget about the whole picture.

92
00:07:04,810 --> 00:07:05,171
[SPEAKER_00]: No, no, no.

93
00:07:05,211 --> 00:07:09,694
[SPEAKER_00]: Let me just forget about the last, the tip of those thoughts,

94
00:07:10,350 --> 00:07:14,993
[SPEAKER_00]: They would kind of give them that momentum and weight through my own mental acceptance of them.

95
00:07:15,713 --> 00:07:17,294
[SPEAKER_00]: But everything else, I mustn't forget.

96
00:07:17,434 --> 00:07:21,076
[SPEAKER_00]: I mustn't forget that I'm still under the liability of those of those pressures.

97
00:07:21,537 --> 00:07:25,819
[SPEAKER_00]: I mustn't forget that I'm still under the liability of lust, aversion, anxiety.

98
00:07:26,359 --> 00:07:31,442
[SPEAKER_00]: Because, see, recognizing liability to a hindrance, it's already a thought.

99
00:07:32,623 --> 00:07:39,227
[SPEAKER_00]: It's already a broader, more general, more peripheral sense of nimitta and characteristics of those states of mind.

100
00:07:39,938 --> 00:07:42,940
[SPEAKER_00]: Even without you waiting to fully experience anxiety or lust.

101
00:07:44,341 --> 00:07:46,023
[SPEAKER_00]: So, now, those thoughts are something you realize.

102
00:07:46,063 --> 00:07:48,084
[SPEAKER_00]: Also, now, I could train in regard to them as well.

103
00:07:48,705 --> 00:07:53,008
[SPEAKER_00]: Those ambiguous, non-defined, yet fully known, in that sense.

104
00:07:53,028 --> 00:07:59,493
[SPEAKER_00]: You know exactly where these... these weird kind of background mood states of mind are leaning towards.

105
00:07:59,593 --> 00:08:04,476
[SPEAKER_00]: You would... if you start... sit down, stop distracting yourself and say, where is this taking me?

106
00:08:04,516 --> 00:08:04,897
[SPEAKER_00]: You would know.

107
00:08:04,917 --> 00:08:07,939
[SPEAKER_00]: It's going to be either lust, desire, restlessness, doubt,

108
00:08:08,973 --> 00:08:10,474
[SPEAKER_00]: Or just laziness and distraction.

109
00:08:10,634 --> 00:08:13,356
[SPEAKER_00]: It's going to be one of the hindrances.

110
00:08:13,977 --> 00:08:14,917
[SPEAKER_00]: So, that's the point.

111
00:08:15,578 --> 00:08:29,467
[SPEAKER_00]: In order to start discerning these broader, even less clear, less defined, less crystallized nimittas, you need to, first and foremost, stop feeding the current ones.

112
00:08:30,568 --> 00:08:34,430
[SPEAKER_00]: Stop grasping the signs and features, how the Sutta says.

113
00:08:35,411 --> 00:08:36,972
[SPEAKER_00]: So, signs and features are always that

114
00:08:37,843 --> 00:08:41,924
[SPEAKER_00]: It's peripheral in regard to whatever you are attending and whatever you're preoccupied with.

115
00:08:42,624 --> 00:08:50,066
[SPEAKER_00]: It's where that pressure is, it's where that contact is, it's where that whole kind of saṅkhara of that activation kind of comes from.

116
00:08:50,986 --> 00:08:55,468
[SPEAKER_00]: You not seeing them, picking them up, you are already under their... under their momentum.

117
00:08:56,688 --> 00:08:58,348
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you can't start from there.

118
00:08:58,388 --> 00:09:04,130
[SPEAKER_00]: You can't just stop them on the level of your mind if your physical behavior is not purified, if your verbal behavior is not purified.

119
00:09:05,022 --> 00:09:17,808
[SPEAKER_00]: But if it were, if it was, then, okay, now this does become a more palpable ground where you could work rightly, where you could recognize the pressure of a lust or a ill will.

120
00:09:19,009 --> 00:09:19,329
[SPEAKER_00]: Feel it.

121
00:09:19,369 --> 00:09:22,670
[SPEAKER_00]: You're going to obviously feel the pressure, because, as I said, you start in reverse order.

122
00:09:23,050 --> 00:09:25,492
[SPEAKER_00]: You don't start being unpressured by hindrance.

123
00:09:25,532 --> 00:09:30,534
[SPEAKER_00]: You're going to feel the pressure and then recognize what thoughts

124
00:09:31,299 --> 00:09:36,461
[SPEAKER_00]: Mind wants to think about, and it's kind of thinking here and there, but without your input.

125
00:09:37,381 --> 00:09:40,062
[SPEAKER_00]: And then it's like, okay, this is still not my problem.

126
00:09:40,082 --> 00:09:44,363
[SPEAKER_00]: I don't have to deal with this, because dealing with this requires me to pick it up, requires me to pick it up.

127
00:09:45,123 --> 00:09:53,986
[SPEAKER_00]: All I need to do is not allow that careless attending to them, that would then carelessly crystallize them, and carelessly feed them further, and give them even more momentum.

128
00:09:54,366 --> 00:09:57,027
[SPEAKER_00]: And if I do, which inevitably you will in the beginning,

129
00:09:57,975 --> 00:10:02,536
[SPEAKER_00]: It's not like, okay, well, now I have to engage with them even more to undo what I did mistakenly.

130
00:10:02,896 --> 00:10:03,036
[SPEAKER_00]: No.

131
00:10:03,677 --> 00:10:10,738
[SPEAKER_00]: At any given point, you catch yourself half an hour caught in the thoughts you shouldn't have been allowing the crystallization and the center stage.

132
00:10:11,479 --> 00:10:15,000
[SPEAKER_00]: At any given point, the principle of withdrawal from them is the same.

133
00:10:15,520 --> 00:10:19,101
[SPEAKER_00]: There and then, when you become self-aware, you don't allow the center stage.

134
00:10:19,141 --> 00:10:19,781
[SPEAKER_00]: You don't allow.

135
00:10:19,861 --> 00:10:23,402
[SPEAKER_00]: You unfocus just to the degree that you were giving them the momentum.

136
00:10:23,942 --> 00:10:24,282
[SPEAKER_00]: That's it.

137
00:10:25,152 --> 00:10:32,354
[SPEAKER_00]: So, it's not... there is... at no point it's justified to pick a hindrance up in order to deal with it.

138
00:10:32,374 --> 00:10:42,518
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's the whole practice of yoniso manasikāra done rightly, whereby it's not about what you're attending, it's about seeing through what the mind wants you to attend.

139
00:10:44,519 --> 00:10:54,242
[SPEAKER_00]: And then, what you are left with is, as the Sutta says, when the hindrances present themselves, but you see through them correctly, you don't pick the signs and features, you don't fall into the trap,

140
00:10:54,898 --> 00:10:58,721
[SPEAKER_00]: What you're left with, in case of lust, is the signs of beautiful.

141
00:10:59,442 --> 00:10:59,942
[SPEAKER_00]: There are not.

142
00:11:00,263 --> 00:11:01,464
[SPEAKER_00]: You have no lust in regard to.

143
00:11:02,084 --> 00:11:03,405
[SPEAKER_00]: The signs of repulsive.

144
00:11:03,686 --> 00:11:05,487
[SPEAKER_00]: You have no ill will in regard to.

145
00:11:06,888 --> 00:11:07,609
[SPEAKER_00]: What was the other one?

146
00:11:07,869 --> 00:11:10,591
[SPEAKER_00]: The things suitable for doubt.

147
00:11:12,713 --> 00:11:14,375
[SPEAKER_00]: Which is still not doubt.

148
00:11:14,675 --> 00:11:20,460
[SPEAKER_00]: Only when you pick it up, when you choose to act out of that pressure, that things suitable for doubt are putting on you.

149
00:11:22,485 --> 00:11:23,586
[SPEAKER_00]: You're still not hindered.

150
00:11:23,606 --> 00:11:30,671
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, the tiredness, it's like wrongly attending to the sign of laziness, to the possibility of not doing anything.

151
00:11:30,691 --> 00:11:32,312
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, dullness.

152
00:11:32,653 --> 00:11:34,634
[SPEAKER_00]: But in and of itself, that's still not a hindrance.

153
00:11:34,674 --> 00:11:43,761
[SPEAKER_00]: The hindrance is when you act out of that initial pressure that they put on you, because the mind is not trained in regard to the pressure.

154
00:11:44,862 --> 00:11:45,182
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's

155
00:11:45,682 --> 00:11:51,003
[SPEAKER_00]: Then, you start evolving and you think you're dealing with them, but in reality, it makes no difference to Mara, as long as you take them.

156
00:11:51,124 --> 00:11:51,344
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

157
00:11:51,444 --> 00:11:55,825
[SPEAKER_00]: You know, whether you go one way or the other way, as long as you first take it, that's all he wants.

158
00:11:56,145 --> 00:11:59,046
[SPEAKER_00]: You are still within his control and the domain.

159
00:12:00,446 --> 00:12:09,969
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you just get more and more aware of the directions that your mind... Is kind of sending you towards.

160
00:12:10,069 --> 00:12:14,190
[SPEAKER_01]: Is pointing towards, but even though it's not in those coarse actions,

161
00:12:15,383 --> 00:12:18,446
[SPEAKER_01]: Just that... just the subtle...

162
00:12:18,646 --> 00:12:19,546
[SPEAKER_01]: The flavor, almost.

163
00:12:19,567 --> 00:12:24,490
[SPEAKER_01]: Tendency, inclination of the mind you could pick up, even though it doesn't seem like just doing anything.

164
00:12:24,871 --> 00:12:26,932
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, well, it's... technically, yeah, exactly.

165
00:12:27,012 --> 00:12:28,974
[SPEAKER_00]: Technically, it's not doing anything, yet.

166
00:12:30,395 --> 00:12:34,118
[SPEAKER_00]: But that doesn't mean that it's not setting up to do those things.

167
00:12:34,378 --> 00:12:36,140
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's what you need to start recognizing.

168
00:12:36,160 --> 00:12:41,624
[SPEAKER_00]: Then again, all the similes about the nimittas and secondary characteristics the Buddha gave in the suttas were exactly that.

169
00:12:41,684 --> 00:12:44,166
[SPEAKER_00]: It's like the cook, the skilled cook,

170
00:12:44,792 --> 00:12:51,213
[SPEAKER_00]: He doesn't just give the food to the king and then forgets where that... where that food kind of led him last time.

171
00:12:52,934 --> 00:12:54,874
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh, he eats this, he doesn't eat it, sometimes he...

172
00:12:55,114 --> 00:12:56,975
[SPEAKER_00]: So, it's like you want to be able to foresee.

173
00:12:57,815 --> 00:13:00,396
[SPEAKER_00]: So, yeah, there's no lust, there's no aversion, there's no doubt.

174
00:13:01,236 --> 00:13:01,876
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, what do I do?

175
00:13:01,956 --> 00:13:05,617
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, recognize that those things are absent and then see.

176
00:13:08,097 --> 00:13:10,818
[SPEAKER_00]: While they're absent, is your mind now leaning towards them?

177
00:13:11,406 --> 00:13:16,209
[SPEAKER_00]: Are you doing things by body, speech, mind, carelessly, that's bringing you closer to them?

178
00:13:17,190 --> 00:13:19,791
[SPEAKER_00]: Because that's already a hindrance.

179
00:13:20,031 --> 00:13:25,735
[SPEAKER_00]: Because it's going to be rooted in some sort of compulsion, in some sort of pressure, however subtle it might be.

180
00:13:27,356 --> 00:13:28,556
[SPEAKER_00]: And as such, it's a hindrance.

181
00:13:28,777 --> 00:13:32,839
[SPEAKER_00]: You're already hindered, even on the level of those possibilities of engagement.

182
00:13:36,581 --> 00:13:39,263
[SPEAKER_00]: If you are not seeing through the nature of those possibilities.

183
00:13:42,567 --> 00:13:58,350
[SPEAKER_01]: This image of having a compass, the right compass, you know exactly what direction you should be going in, what direction you shouldn't be going in, like a... maybe like a captain on a boat, you know, because just a little bit, a degree off.

184
00:13:58,610 --> 00:13:58,811
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

185
00:13:59,171 --> 00:14:03,372
[SPEAKER_01]: It looks like you're going to to a certain island, but it's actually a degree off.

186
00:14:03,932 --> 00:14:05,732
[SPEAKER_00]: Of course, like, it will be.

187
00:14:06,912 --> 00:14:09,833
[SPEAKER_00]: It's not going to be absolutely 100% accurate from the start.

188
00:14:09,993 --> 00:14:10,333
[SPEAKER_00]: It's like

189
00:14:10,885 --> 00:14:18,691
[SPEAKER_00]: Through trial and error and refinement, you're getting a more accurate and accurate reading as to, like, the signs and features.

190
00:14:18,711 --> 00:14:20,552
[SPEAKER_00]: You're becoming even more skilled cook.

191
00:14:21,153 --> 00:14:27,898
[SPEAKER_00]: You recognize three days ahead what the king will want, type of thing, where the king's preferences are heading.

192
00:14:28,238 --> 00:14:30,380
[SPEAKER_00]: So that's that's kind of the whole the whole point.

193
00:14:30,420 --> 00:14:33,542
[SPEAKER_00]: But as I said, it's not like you have to do something.

194
00:14:34,300 --> 00:14:35,781
[SPEAKER_00]: On account of it, any different thing.

195
00:14:35,921 --> 00:14:40,765
[SPEAKER_00]: It's... the problem is in you not recognizing in the first place and then doing everything else but the thing you should do.

196
00:14:41,466 --> 00:15:01,422
[SPEAKER_00]: And thing you should do is abstain from doing anything on account of picking up the pressure and instead recognize that whenever there is a pressure of any hindrance, lust, aversion, laziness, restlessness, anxiety, doubt, whenever there is a pressure of any hindrance, there is associated thoughts

197
00:15:02,192 --> 00:15:07,054
[SPEAKER_00]: They want to take the center stage of your attention, of your mind, want to run the show.

198
00:15:08,415 --> 00:15:10,216
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's what you don't do.

199
00:15:10,316 --> 00:15:15,198
[SPEAKER_00]: I won't give them that last satisfaction of mentally, OK, let me take this up.

200
00:15:15,478 --> 00:15:15,859
[SPEAKER_00]: That's it.

201
00:15:17,079 --> 00:15:29,045
[SPEAKER_00]: But see, that's quite a hard thing to do, especially in the beginning, where your whole being depends on doing and managing and fighting and defending yourself from these pressures that arise.

202
00:15:29,833 --> 00:15:35,918
[SPEAKER_00]: But you inadvertently, by dealing, by acting out of a pressure, you're inadvertently affirming it.

203
00:15:35,958 --> 00:15:38,880
[SPEAKER_00]: You're inadvertently picking up what a pressure is serving you with.

204
00:15:39,200 --> 00:15:43,143
[SPEAKER_00]: And then you try to counter it with with a subha or with metta or with this.

205
00:15:43,564 --> 00:15:44,384
[SPEAKER_00]: And it never works.

206
00:15:46,686 --> 00:15:47,647
[SPEAKER_00]: Because you're picking it up.

207
00:15:48,588 --> 00:15:56,574
[SPEAKER_00]: But if you don't pick it up, then the subha is discerned on the level of that possibility of the beauty, without you needing to pick it up.

208
00:15:56,594 --> 00:15:59,416
[SPEAKER_00]: Because beautiful is already factually ugly.

209
00:16:00,829 --> 00:16:03,652
[SPEAKER_00]: You don't need to pick up the beautiful to prove to yourself that it's ugly.

210
00:16:04,172 --> 00:16:08,316
[SPEAKER_00]: You just need to not pick it up, stay long enough with it, and you'll discern the ugliness.

211
00:16:08,336 --> 00:16:09,337
[SPEAKER_00]: That's exactly what the Sutta says.

212
00:16:09,778 --> 00:16:12,861
[SPEAKER_00]: Within the sign of subha, he sees a subha.

213
00:16:14,322 --> 00:16:16,824
[SPEAKER_00]: And if he becomes skilled in that, then he can see it either way.

214
00:16:17,225 --> 00:16:18,826
[SPEAKER_00]: Within a subha, he can see subha.

215
00:16:21,008 --> 00:16:22,069
[SPEAKER_00]: Not at the expense of it.

216
00:16:22,129 --> 00:16:23,631
[SPEAKER_00]: Not replacing one with the other.

217
00:16:23,791 --> 00:16:24,532
[SPEAKER_01]: Just seeing through.

218
00:16:24,592 --> 00:16:25,653
[SPEAKER_00]: He sees the whole extent.

219
00:16:25,773 --> 00:16:25,933
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

